# --- credentials: never commit.
# A machine-global excludesfile on the author's machine covers most of this too,
# but a global ignore does NOT travel with a clone. This repo is going public, so
# it carries its own list and does not rely on anyone's machine being set up.
gurobi.lic
*.lic
*.lic.*
# *.lic alone does not match a RENAMED licence file - gurobi.lic.aside,
# gurobi.lic.bak, gurobi.lic.old. Renaming one aside to reproduce a
# restricted-licence run is a normal thing to do and it silently drops the
# file out of the ignore. Second instance of this pattern class today:
# *.bak likewise missed dispatch-template.zip.bak-2026-09-04.
*WLSKeyinfo*
.env
.env.*
*.env
.secrets/
service-account*.json

# --- solver / build noise
gurobi.log
*.lp
*.mps
*.sol
*.ilp
*.attr

# --- python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# --- os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pre-rebase.bak
# *.bak alone does NOT match a dated backup like foo.zip.bak-2026-09-04,
# which is the convention used when the template zips were rebuilt.

# --- generated results. results/figures IS tracked on purpose (see README).
results/tables/*
!results/tables/.gitkeep

# --- pytest
.pytest_cache/

# --- the notebook's loud no-data fallback writes here; never a real instance
_generated_fallback/
notebooks/_generated_fallback/

# --- stale copies of the portable standard. The source is
# Classes/Code Standard (-> sear-labs/code-standard); CLAUDE.md Parts 0-10
# here are synced FROM it. These two are 577-line snapshots, referenced by
# nothing, and shipping them would publish three versions of one document.
# Files stay on disk; they are just not this repo's to distribute.
Code and Teaching Standard (portable).md
dispatch-template.zip
